        "problem": "Find $f''(x)$ for $f(x) = 2x^3 + \\dfrac 1 x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{x})}^{\u2032} \\\\  & ={(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{-1})}^{\u2032} \\\\  & =2(3){x}^{2}-{x}^{-2} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2033}(x) & =(6{x}^{2}-{x}^{-2})^{\u2032} \\\\  & =6(2)x-(-2){x}^{-3} \\\\  & =12x+2{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
